# Kang, Suspicious Captain: the counter goes on a creature Bot1 controls. Kang enters on turn 3 and goads Bot2's Llanowar
# Elves; on turn 4 that goaded creature must attack (CR 701.15b) and the attack fires "whenever one or more goaded
# creatures attack" (CR 508.1, 603.2c). Kang is then Bot1's only creature, the only legal target, so the counter lands on
# it. Grizzly Bears joins on turn 5, so Kang's own goaded attack that turn offers a real choice: Bot2's Elves, a creature
# Bot1 does not control, is refused, and the counter goes on the Bears (CR 601.2c, 608.2b). The Elves attack again on turn
# 6 and the choice is taken the other way, so each creature has exactly one +1/+1 counter: one counter per combat, one
# point each, not two.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Kang, Suspicious Captain
Mountain
Grizzly Bears
Mountain x2
Mountain x12

